This is a **test fixture**, not a real application. It's a deliberately tiny project used to verify OpenCode's "Phase 4 production-host gates" — giving file-search tools (glob, read, ripgrep) and git operations something small and predictable to exercise against.

### Structure

```
gates/
├── README.md          # Project description, contains G15-E2E-MARKER
├── g8-write.txt       # Untracked file with G8_WRITE_OK (write-gate test)
├── notes.txt          # Contains G15-E2E-MARKER (ripgrep target)
└── src/
    └── app.js         # Single ES module exporting greet(name)
```

### Key details

- **4 tracked files, 1 untracked** (`g8-write.txt`)
- **Marker strings** (`G15-E2E-MARKER`, `G8_WRITE_OK`) are embedded so gates can verify search/find/write operations produce expected results
- **Git state**: one commit on `main`, plus a `feature/g9` branch with a diff — exists so git/grep gates can test branch and cross-branch operations
- **No dependencies, no build system, no tests** — the `greet()` function is never actually run

It exists purely so the OpenCode toolchain has known inputs with expected outputs to validate against during gate checks.
